@startuml development-view
' 4+1 — DEVELOPMENT VIEW: source module organization and reuse.
title 4+1 Development View — .bob/skills/ai-factory-executor

skinparam packageStyle folder
left to right direction

package "ai-factory-executor (existing)" as EXE {
  [Dockerfile.agent] as DF
  [agent-entrypoint.ps1] as ENTRY
  [experiment-entrypoint.ps1]
  [pr-monitor.ps1]
  [run-factory.ps1] <<retired by Argo>>
  [container-manager.ps1] <<local fallback>>
}

package "argo/ (new)" as ARGO {
  [implement-issue.ps1] <<entry point>> as CLI
  [install.ps1] as INSTALL
  package "manifests" {
    [workflowtemplate-agent.yaml] as WT
    [semaphore-config.yaml] as SEM
    [networkpolicy.yaml]
    [rbac.yaml]
  }
  package "deferred trigger" as DEF {
    [workflowtemplate-dispatcher.yaml]
    [eventsource.yaml]
    [sensor.yaml]
    [scripts/dispatch.ps1]
  }
  package "diagrams" {
    [c4/*]
    [views/*]
  }
}

CLI ..> WT : argo submit --from
INSTALL ..> WT : kubectl apply
INSTALL ..> DF : docker build + import
WT ..> DF : image: ai-factory-agent
WT ..> ENTRY : container command
WT ..> SEM : semaphore ref
DEF ..> WT : (optional) submits

note bottom of EXE
Reused as-is. The Dockerfile image and
agent-entrypoint.ps1 need no changes —
their env + /run/secrets contract maps
straight onto the k8s pod spec.
end note

@enduml
